I go into a phone shop.
There is a man in the shop.
He says, "Hi."
He asks, "How can I help you?"
"I need a Danish phone number," I say.
The man is friendly, and he helps me.
I get a small card with my new number.
I read the number aloud to him.
I say slowly: "Twelve ..."
"... thirty-four ..."
"... fifty-six ..."
"... seventy-eight."
Now I have a phone number in Denmark.
